        "original_id": "221b09bc-6d5a-5653-af1c-79c10017e5ac",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Chas Chandler, John Constantine, Alan Moore, Steve Bissette, John Totleben, Jamie Delano, Philip Bond\n- Roles: sidekick, cab driver, friend, writer, illustrator, creator, antihero\n- Organizations: DC Comics, Vertigo\n- Products: Hellblazer Special: Bad Blood, comic books\n- Concepts: fictional character, series continuity\n\nFacts:\n- John Constantine is a fictional antihero who appears in comic books published by DC Comics and its alternative imprint Vertigo.\n- John Constantine was created in 1984 in Swamp Thing No. 25 by Alan Moore, Steve Bissette, and John Totleben.\n- Chas Chandler is John Constantine's closest and longest surviving friend, and he acts as Constantine's sidekick and cab driver.\n- Hellblazer Special: Bad Blood was written by Jamie Delano and illustrated by Philip Bond.\n- Hellblazer Special: Bad Blood features John Constantine several decades after most of his series continuity.",
